        "original_id": "f212e67c-58ac-5215-b18d-36412a5e5ed6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Conrad Aiken, Mahatma Gandhi\n- Works: \"Silent Snow, Secret Snow\"\n- Topics: American literature, Indian independence movement\n\nFacts:\n- Mahatma Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi was born on 2 October 1869 and died on 30 January 1948.\n- Mahatma Gandhi was the leader of the Indian independence movement against British rule.\n- Conrad Potter Aiken was born on August 5, 1889 and died on August 17, 1973.\n- Conrad Aiken was an American writer whose work included poetry, short stories, novels, a play, and an autobiography.\n- \"Silent Snow, Secret Snow\" was published in 1934.\n- \"Silent Snow, Secret Snow\" is Conrad Aiken's best-known short story.\n- \"Silent Snow, Secret Snow\" is often included in anthologies of classic American horror and fantasy short fiction.",
